## Why This Is Asked

Tests practical monitoring and defense against credential stuffing in a multi-tenant context, focusing on observable signals, mitigations, and operator visibility.

## Key Concepts

- Per-IP and per-tenant rate limiting
- Sliding window counters
- MFA enforcement for risk
- Centralized logging and alerts
- Synthetic traffic validation

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-code for login rate limiter using Redis
const { RateLimiterRedis } = require('rate-limiter-flexible');
const redisClient = require('redis').createClient();

const limiter = new RateLimiterRedis({
  points: 5, // attempts
  duration: 60, // per 60s
  storeClient: redisClient
});

// In login route
async function login(req, res) {
  try {
    await limiter.consume(req.ip);
    // authentication logic
    res.send('OK');
  } catch {
    res.status(429).send('Too many attempts');
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you tune thresholds for users behind shared proxies?
- How would you test rate limiter behavior under burst traffic and production latency constraints?

